{"id":"e587212f956744893c6492592ca6cc367aa90437","axis":"silent","repo":"symfony/symfony","sha":"e587212f956744893c6492592ca6cc367aa90437","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"src/Symfony/Component/KeyManagement/Bridge/Kmip/Kmip/ProtocolVersion.php","lines":["@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@","  * KMIP 1.2 and 1.3 define those operations but not the Authenticated Encryption Tag or Authenticated Encryption Additional Data payload fields introduced in 1.4.","  * The tag lets Decrypt detect changed ciphertext. The additional data field carries the caller's AAD so that it is authenticated without being encrypted. Without these fields, the bridge cannot verify its authenticated ciphertext or reject decryption with different AAD.","  *","- * The bridge supports its single-part Encrypt and Decrypt flow on 1.4 and 2.0.","+ * The bridge supports its single-part Encrypt and Decrypt flow on 1.4, 2.0 and 2.1.","  *","  * @author Antonio Pauletich <antonio.pauletich95@gmail.com>","  *","@@ -28,4 +28,5 @@ enum ProtocolVersion: string"," {","     case Version14 = '1.4';","     case Version20 = '2.0';","+    case Version21 = '2.1';"," }"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Component/KeyManagement/Bridge/Kmip/Kmip/Ttlv.php","lines":["@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@","  * Encoding pads items to that alignment.","  * Decoding checks item boundaries, tag prefixes, type lengths, Boolean values and UTF-8 text before returning the raw item values.","  *","- * The decoder accepts the Date Time Extended type only for KMIP 2.0. It checks TTLV syntax; {@see ProtocolClient} checks the meaning and order of fields in KMIP responses.","+ * The decoder accepts the Date Time Extended type only for KMIP 2.0 and 2.1. It checks TTLV syntax; {@see ProtocolClient} checks the meaning and order of fields in KMIP responses.","  *","  * @author Antonio Pauletich <antonio.pauletich95@gmail.com>","  *"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Component/KeyManagement/Bridge/Kmip/KmipKmsFactory.php","lines":["@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@","  * The `ca` option names a certificate authority file used to verify the server certificate; omitting it uses the system trust store.","  * The `peer_name` option controls the expected server name. The DSN has no path.","  *","- * The KMIP version, 1.4 or 2.0, must be selected explicitly. The `iv_length` option sets the AES-GCM IV length of new ciphertexts, 12 bytes by default.","+ * The KMIP version, 1.4, 2.0 or 2.1, must be selected explicitly. The `iv_length` option sets the AES-GCM IV length of new ciphertexts, 12 bytes by default.","  *","  * @author Antonio Pauletich <antonio.pauletich95@gmail.com>","  *"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Component/KeyManagement/Bridge/Kmip/README.md","lines":["@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@ kmip://[<username>:<password>@]<host>[:<port>]?cert=<client-cert-file>&key=<clie"," timeout to 10 seconds. Supply both username and password or neither, and"," percent-encode reserved characters in credentials and option values."," ","-The bridge supports KMIP 1.4 and 2.0 for authenticated Encrypt and Decrypt.","+The bridge supports KMIP 1.4, 2.0 and 2.1 for authenticated Encrypt and Decrypt."," Select the server's version in the DSN. KMIP 1.0 and 1.1 lack Encrypt and"," Decrypt; 1.2 and 1.3 lack the authentication tag and associated data fields"," required by this bridge."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Component/KeyManagement/Bridge/Kmip/Tests/Fixtures/KmipWireExamples.php","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@ final class KmipWireExamples","     public const int GET_REQUEST_VERSION14 = 8;","     public const int GET_RESPONSE_VERSION14 = 9;"," ","+    public const int DECRYPT_RESPONSE_VERSION21 = 10;","+    public const int ENCRYPT_REQUEST_VERSION21 = 11;","+    public const int ENCRYPT_RESPONSE_VERSION21 = 12;","+","     private const array HEX = [","         self::DISCOVER_VERSIONS_REQUEST_VERSION14 => '4200780100000060420077010000003842006901